#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501261} :activity/id #uuid "948eb367-d5fd-51df-b125-e3149e49d0c4" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048656 :topic/id #uuid "b2c975cf-4aab-5305-b223-4eaed44fd857" :topic/math-academy-id 3338} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501261 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172655 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06716dfe-08a6-516e-a629-177bb828c2fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=-3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi t\\,j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500479} {:answer/id #uuid "31e995dd-ff4a-5e6d-8cf4-3bfb96a6017b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi t\\,j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500571} {:answer/id #uuid "3f2848b3-8ddd-5fb7-95ae-348cf52cb0ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\pi t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\pi t\\,j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500591} {:answer/id #uuid "be530a2a-8d30-591a-8cf9-2082ebebbbb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi t\\,j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500863} {:answer/id #uuid "f0a4ff08-122d-5fd6-b066-879bdb9fa494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=-2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\pi t\\,j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500978}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500571} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa2448a5-0101-5a28-982e-8f121a6f37a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171555}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "297d89f1-479f-5e7e-834d-0ffc08d592cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-97586" :question/problem "A particle moves along a **clockwise** circular path with center $O$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity of $2\\pi \\text{ rad/s}.$ Given that the object is at the position $(3,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the position function of the particle." :question/worked-solution "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nSince the object's initial position is $(3,0),$ we have that $r(0)=\\,3i,$ and we can conclude that the radius of the circle $R=3.$\n\nTherefore, since we have $R=3$ and $\\omega =-2\\pi \\text{ rad/s}$ (negative because the motion is clockwise), we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-2\\pi t)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi t)\\,j) \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "368577ca-f476-5cfa-9e6b-273c753b6b1a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501282}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501270 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501234 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a682535-8c56-55dd-a035-f6b7cc19fc38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "54\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500486} {:answer/id #uuid "6f323c8b-a972-54d0-bbd1-34949e7b25d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500694} {:answer/id #uuid "7be1cdf9-0f94-5f70-8486-f5416dfcc558" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "81\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500724} {:answer/id #uuid "98ff3c6b-5897-5008-9dfd-a379593dd6c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500779} {:answer/id #uuid "a385d26b-a169-54eb-af49-c35e70069687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "27\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500796}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500796} :answer-field/id #uuid "4264e826-1eca-5166-bc99-fe720168444a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ea3775f0-4a19-53d1-b4e1-4eb3518e099f" :question/math-academy-id "q-97670" :question/problem "An object moves along a circular path with position $r(t)=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,j)$ meters. Find the magnitude of the acceleration of the object at time $t,$ measured in seconds." :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(r(t))^{′} \\\\  & =(3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,j))^{′} \\\\  & =-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,i+9\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the acceleration vector by differentiating the velocity vector. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =(v(t))^{′} \\\\  & =(-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,i+9\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,j)^{′} \\\\  & =-27\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,i-27\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the magnitude of the acceleration as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}||a(t)|| & =\\sqrt{(-27\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)^{2}+(-27\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{27}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡3t+{27}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡3t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{27}^{2}} \\\\  & =27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude of the acceleration is $27\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nNote that $||a||$ is constant, but $a$ is not. \n\n**Method 2**\n\nFor uniform circular motion in the $xy$-plane, we have\n\n$$\na=-{\\omega }^{2}r\\,⇒\\,||a||={\\omega }^{2}||r||.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the radius of the circle is $a=3\\,\\text{m}$ and the angular frequency $\\omega =3\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n||a||={3}^{2}\\cdot 3=27\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "5c6597e4-8215-5ac5-9944-f088aeed0bde"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501272 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501167 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05373043-ede4-5f3b-ab00-6c5eb28bd928" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500476} {:answer/id #uuid "43f6eebb-f90b-5e3e-bf7f-5a7b4d0e7ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500601} {:answer/id #uuid "510f8649-056c-567e-b3ee-8b8aa7b327bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500633} {:answer/id #uuid "9cde80f5-0a17-51cc-8fcb-e28702d3897c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500785} {:answer/id #uuid "e33da50a-6797-5e61-8dad-558084c1c0d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500950}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500950} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f20aec0-879d-5670-bfea-c9c0def60bdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5b5c204f-7839-5ec6-95c0-a9151439158a" :question/math-academy-id "q-97637" :question/problem "A particle moves along a **clockwise** circular path with center $O$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\text{ rad/s}.$ Given that the object is at the position $(1,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the position function of the particle." :question/worked-solution "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nSince the object's initial position is $(1,0),$ we have that $r(0)=\\,1i,$ and we can conclude that the radius of the circle $R=1.$\n\nTherefore, since we have $R=1$ and $\\omega =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\text{ rad/s}$ (negative because the motion is clockwise), we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7068fb21-64e6-51f4-b3a5-0162c383a600" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501270}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501282 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362221 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cd02180-7f22-5f61-93c7-fff08cd0fa7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360952} {:answer/id #uuid "3ad8a471-2d04-5600-9388-bfbdf3391f3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361105} {:answer/id #uuid "75a3c33c-0bca-5f44-a5b5-84ee07be1813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361356} {:answer/id #uuid "845ab6b4-5c02-5255-a705-c026ab5d4e0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361427} {:answer/id #uuid "b0e84a90-a66f-5f65-ad44-888c40336abc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361622}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360952} :answer-field/id #uuid "87b5905c-bd9f-57b9-8aca-d92b2a486288" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4a58d6f2-a102-5329-9df6-5ca2570034eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-97631" :question/problem "A particle moves along a circular path centered at $O$ in the $xy$-plane in the counterclockwise direction with a constant angular velocity of $1\\text{ rad/s}.$ Given that the object is at the position $(4,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the position function of the particle." :question/worked-solution "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nSince the object's initial position is $(4,0),$ we have that $r(0)=4i,$ and we can conclude that the circle's radius is $R=4.$\n\nTherefore, since we have $R=4$ and $\\omega =1\\text{ rad/s},$ we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b298bba9-5caf-53be-a1b8-5e5bfe3389e9" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501289}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501289 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362222 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "029a7f99-f667-5979-a59f-0e86cfa31195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\,j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360840} {:answer/id #uuid "5407564b-be54-5b7e-b365-08c7dd2979bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡8t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡8t\\,j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361209} {:answer/id #uuid "aed4d295-17ee-5234-8841-738be0c227d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\,j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361610} {:answer/id #uuid "ba462204-6404-53bb-a653-40fd5d5fc0bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361667} {:answer/id #uuid "fada0c54-2f8f-5502-bc13-443d0123345e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r(t)=4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡8t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡8t\\,j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361958}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186361610} :answer-field/id #uuid "bff7f1a0-ee8f-51c5-b306-5103d68b521c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0696e9be-8b02-58ba-8734-5aa777937265" :question/math-academy-id "q-97632" :question/problem "A particle moves along a circular path centered at $O$ in the $xy$-plane in the counterclockwise direction with a constant angular velocity of $4\\text{ rad/s}.$ Given that the object is at the position $(8,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the position function of the particle." :question/worked-solution "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nSince the object's initial position is $(8,0),$ we have that $r(0)=8i,$ and we can conclude that the circle's radius is $R=8.$\n\nTherefore, since we have $R=8$ and $\\omega =4\\text{ rad/s},$ we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c62d5c7d-4f34-5f60-92b7-d492ba362088" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501272}}] :activity/title "Circular Motion About the Origin" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500464}]}
